      "side": 1,
      "message": "In theory the deleted virtual methods can be reintroduced as virtual methods of the `Context` (because right now functions like [`LibPngDecoder::ContinueDecode`](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/pdfium/core/fxcodec/png/libpng_png_decoder.cpp;l\u003d209-217;drc\u003d8900162810d457b64286ce653cb61bc2009c5068) or [`BmpDecoder::Input`](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/pdfium/core/fxcodec/bmp/bmp_decoder.cpp;l\u003d65-71;drc\u003d8900162810d457b64286ce653cb61bc2009c5068) are kind of manually doing a virtual dispatch [except that caller guarantees which virtual table is being used]).\n\nBut...\n\n* Let\u0027s do this step-by-step (the CL under review still makes sense on its own - removing an unneeded layer of indirection;  here we are talking about a different layer of calls)\n* I am not sure if doing virtual dispatch is needed at all.  I guess a `virtual` dispatch would avoid a `static_cast` in [`LibPngDecoder::ContinueDecode`](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/pdfium/core/fxcodec/png/libpng_png_decoder.cpp;l\u003d209-217;drc\u003d8900162810d457b64286ce653cb61bc2009c5068) or [`BmpDecoder::Input`](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/pdfium/core/fxcodec/bmp/bmp_decoder.cpp;l\u003d65-71;drc\u003d8900162810d457b64286ce653cb61bc2009c5068).  But `ProgressiveDecoder` already knows which decoder it is working with (well, except for libpng-vs-Rust-PNG).  So if it wasn\u0027t for libpng-vs-Rust-PNG we could get rid of `Context` altogether (just have `StartDecoding` return a concrete class).\n\nSo, I think that I may end up renaming `ProgressiveDecoderIface::Context` into `ProgressiveDecoderContext` (the TODO captured here), but won\u0027t be doing any of the other follow-up I am mentioning above (because it doesn\u0027t seem to be needed that much + because I am not sure about the best long-term shape for things - what we have works ok).",
